+# R27 final-plan repair contract1 — 2026-10-28
+
+This sourced increment applies to `FinalPlanRepair`, `TaskPlanner.accept/repairFinalPlan` and `AgentTaskStore.returnedResult` on the isolated R27-06–09 candidate based at 070f3d83c294ba0d4a2197d591055e75cff59ac3. Exact filesystem/source/index/APK hashes belong to `HXai_CHANGE_REVIEW/R27-06-FINALPLAN-20261028/`. It supplements the original Pro new-feature/full-review gates without editing or lowering them.
+
+The original ChatService → ConversationSession → GenerationLoop → TaskPlanner remains the only executor. The final phase happens while its original lease/model/source guard is active, before normal whole-goal acceptance. It never dispatches a new tool, acquires another task slot or turns a rejected certificate into proof.
+
+Repair is eligible only with nonempty acceptance, current goal revision, at least one VERIFIED step, bounded persisted evidence (262144 characters including inputs), and no PLANNED/IN_FLIGHT/UNKNOWN step. Unverified actions are eligible only when they are settled math_verify DISPROVED/UNSUPPORTED results. Every Room tool receipt matches the persisted step and input-bound call; rejected math is independently recomputed. The other eligible defect is an artifact predicate on Text output when actual VERIFIED Document producers exist.
+
+A single request under the already accepted main model/reasoning and existing planning accounting role proposes a final plan (`HXAI_FINAL_PLAN_V1`). It sees the complete unchanged goal and actual bounded evidence. The host requires exactly the existing VERIFIED step IDs/tools, with no omissions or new dispatch slots; artifact predicates must reference actual Document-producing steps. A malformed or incomplete proposal remains unverified. Every physical request has its own ledger ID; no price/token budget or model fallback is introduced.
+
+Before physical dispatch and after reply, the original source guard, owner/task/fence/grant epoch, journal binding and independent tool readbacks are checked again. Existing publishPlan transaction preserves VERIFIED rows and rejects unresolved calls. It removes superseded RETURNED rows only from the active plan; immutable call rows/Room history remain rejected. Actual artifacts/source hashes and the separate evidence-hash/goal-revision-bound semantic evaluator must still satisfy the entire original goal. Nothing is completed solely because plan repair returned JSON.
+
+Whole-goal evidence also carries every settled rejected mathematical call in the current task, including calls omitted by an earlier replan or a final plan persisted before interruption. Each call ID/input hash/current grant/durable result is rebound to the actual Room receipt and independently recomputed. It is explicitly labeled `settled_rejected_math_not_proof`; a replacement proof does not make the rejected original certificate valid or satisfy a required false claim, and a failed certificate does not refute its target. The same history is checked before semantic dispatch and after reply. At most 64 rejected calls and the bounded new projection are admitted; overflow is preserved/unverified, never truncated. Existing ordinary all-VERIFIED tasks without rejected math history retain their previous projection behavior.
+
+Room33, TaskStore13, tool risk registry, Pigeon/DTO, UI task states, authorization, manual pause and device/input blockers are unchanged. No migration is required. The existing usage role `planning` also avoids adding an unrecognized UI role. New phase metadata is test evidence, not user authority.
+
+The opt-in native QA helper may seed a new public evaluation from a successful previous QA task's encrypted immutable configuration, only after checking configuration hash, exact provider/API model/reasoning/Responses selection and no IN_FLIGHT/UNKNOWN source calls. It does not resume or replay that task, export its key, migrate product credentials or restore revoked grants. The old one-shot provisioning route remains. Both routes require the existing explicit public-call consent/nativeqa package gates.
+
+The process-death driver adds optional new output/APK-manifest paths; its five actual process stops and exact installed APK checks remain unchanged. Default historical paths remain compatible. No real user Office instance, production deployment or unauthorized private document is involved.
+
+Rollback this exact code delta in isolation while preserving plans/calls/model snapshots/usage/material versions and unknown intents. A downgrade cannot turn retained rejected math into verified evidence. Independent/full-project review remains NOT_EVALUATED unless explicitly supported by a separately recorded complete scope; this batch's developer checks are identified as same executor.
+
+Every VERIFIED exact-math step now contributes its actual formal input, call ID, raw dispatch SHA256 and durable verifier result to whole-goal evidence, even if no acceptance predicate names it. The actual Room receipt/output must match the task journal and pass independent recomputation. Recheck it before physical semantic dispatch and after the reply; a hash or assumption ID without its premise formula cannot establish correspondence with the original problem. Canonical verifier input hashes and raw dispatch hashes remain distinct. The old native absent-input refusal is preserved before this repair.
+
+The opt-in public QA observer clones the original OpenAIProvider HTTP client and adds one observational interceptor, restoring the original provider on close. It dispatches no extra request, changes no provider reply, omits hidden reasoning/headers, redacts known credentials and caps exported coordinator message text. Its optional receipt-bound files are diagnostic evidence, not model authentication. The offline importer rejects changed bytes, unsafe/duplicate names and excessive/missing observation files; older exports without this optional list remain supported.
+
+The complete 37-case pre-binary-fix cohort exposed a supplemental plot PNG being sent to MaterialReader's text reader. For png/jpg/jpeg/webp only, artifactEvidence now retains all actual owner/output/source/hash checks and contributes explicit binary-only metadata with content=null and visual content NOT_EVALUATED. It does not invent extracted text, authenticate appearance or prove mathematics. Existing supported artifact-predicate formats and risk gates are unchanged; this metadata cannot satisfy a missing visual requirement. Text/Office/PDF readback and malformed/unknown formats still follow the existing reader. The old native failure and exact pre-fix APK/source cohort remain separate from final scoped post-fix regressions; the 37 paid cases are not relabeled or replayed as later-source results.
