+# R29 response delivery / original Office request readback v1
+
+Based on b0ed6acc7c2a03df0a28e80f6c07d82a44e35d45 in the existing isolated R27-06–09 branch. Source contracts: `HXai_CHANGE_REVIEW/R29-06-RESPONSE-CONTRACT-20261029/CHANGE_CONTRACT.md` and `OFFICE_RECOVERY_CONTRACT.md`. Original Pro standards and failed evidence remain intact; independent/full review is NOT_EVALUATED.
+
+ChatService → ConversationSession → GenerationLoop → TaskPlanner → TaskStore remains the sole executor. The final DurableCheckpoint waits for the conflated consumer to commit. ConversationRepository independently reads the selected reply in the original incarnation and active owner; it checks generationTaskId, actual parts, finishedAt and modelId. The source Room transaction also covers the final sidecar publication, so a branch/delete cannot slip between that read and commit.
+
+ResponseCompletion accepts bounded finished assistant text/reasoning only. TaskStore.responseEligible rejects non-provider calls, unresolved provider requests, old tool steps or non-response predicates. Settled provider calls keep their original accounting. The same locked configuration performs one accounted semantic_acceptance request, HXAI_RESPONSE_DISPOSITION_V1. Evidence binds owner/task/conversation/message, complete parts SHA, visible text, goal SHA/revision, fence/grantEpoch and provider/model/reasoning/config revision; source/lease/bytes are checked before physical dispatch and after return.
+
+Strict decision fields distinguish delivered, needs_input and unverified, bind exact revision/hash, and quote actual visible text. Delivery requires no independent-evidence requirement and certifies text delivery only. evidence_json explicitly records mathematics_status NOT_EVALUATED. Semantic classification uses the same selected model and is fallible: synthetic tests cannot certify real mathematical accuracy. Files, formal proofs, citations and external effects retain their original verifier requirements. A correct textual refutation is not a mathematical certificate.
+
+response_delivery has reserved _response, one digest, no steps/source/format. Ordinary acceptGoal rejects this predicate, preventing plan-only completion. recordResponse rechecks current goal, owner/model/grant/fence and settled journal. needs_input only sets input_blocked with its evidence and quoted request; success stays false. finish releases the slot only after safe settlement. Explicit provide_input increments the goal revision and invalidates acceptance, preserving other blockers/manual pause. UI shows the delivery scope when a no-step task is accepted.
+
+GET /api/v1/conversion-requests/{request_key} and /recalculation-requests/{request_key} authenticate and recheck active identity in Store.read_request's read transaction. They never enqueue, cancel or change retention/renderers. Wrong owner/operation/unobserved requests yield 404; revoked identity yields 401. Current renderer readiness is irrelevant. The reply binds original requestKey/sourceSha256/sourceExtension/operation/rendererVersion/taskId/state.
+
+OfficeConversionRepository.submit with an existing SUBMITTING intent, resume, and refresh without remoteId only GET that original request. Original config/request/source and post-response local bytes must match. A 404/network failure never proves absence and never triggers reupload. Current capability version cannot replace the original job version. Missing renderer metadata preserves recovered remoteId with renderer_receipt_incomplete and prevents artifact publication. Existing source/manifest/output SHA and independent file readback still apply. Cancellation retains its original protocol.
+
+Room33, TaskStore13, Pigeon and Office intent serialization do not migrate. The constrained AgentPlan predicate is an additive protocol; old plans remain readable. Disable new response acceptance/unknown-intent resume before reversing the delta; preserve all evidence/UNKNOWN/grants/materials and a compatible reader for response_delivery records. Do not downgrade data or reupload on rollback. Existing deployed services need an authorized rollout/read query; local code does not resolve the historical remote job.
+
+Source map: GenerationLoop.generateText; ChatService.handleMessageComplete; ConversationRepository.readTaskResponse/commitTaskResponse; TaskPlanner.accept/acceptResponse; ResponseCompletion; AgentPlan.validate; AgentTaskStore.responseEligible/recordResponse/acceptGoal; Flutter task detail scope note; OfficeConversionRepository.submit/resume/refresh/readOriginalRequest; document-service api/office.register_office and api/store.Store.read_request. Tests: ResponseCompletionTest, ResponseCompletionRuntimeTest/StoreTest/ProcessProbe, existing AgentTaskRuntimeTest/MathSharedChatRuntimeTest/OfficeConversionRepositoryTest and service test_request_readback.py. Process driver adds optional response_wait/response_delivery; original five remain default. Exact results/source/APK cohorts belong to TEST_RESULTS and SOURCE_FINAL.
